  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Can I read fuel level remotely on an Audi Q5?",
      "a": "Yes, with a DIMO device. Fuel level is available in liters and as a percentage through the Telemetry API, which you query with a Vehicle JWT. To find refuel events, use the segments query with the refuel detection mechanism, which detects where fuel level rises significantly."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I track an Audi Q5 with no connected services?",
      "a": "Connect a DIMO device to the vehicle and have the owner share it with your Developer License. Then exchange your Developer JWT for a Vehicle JWT through the Token Exchange API and query the vehicle in the Telemetry API."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I get check-engine light alerts for an Audi Q5?",
      "a": "Yes, with a DIMO device, which lists the dtc event for this vehicle. The Vehicle Triggers API (webhooks) sends a POST request to your target URL in real time when a condition you configure is met, so you don't have to poll."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect idling on an Audi Q5?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device and the Telemetry API segments query with the idling detection mechanism, which finds contiguous periods where engine RPM stays in the idle range. You can adjust the idle RPM ceiling with the maxIdleRpm setting; the default is 1000."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I verify Audi Q5 mileage?",
      "a": "With a DIMO device supplying the odometer signal, call the Attestation API odometer-statement endpoint with a Vehicle JWT. It generates a verifiable odometer attestation that you can retrieve through the Telemetry API."
    }
  ],
  "intro": "DIMO provides a vehicle data API for the Audi Q5, which connects through a DIMO device for model years 2009 and newer. Coverage for this vehicle was tested. DIMO gives developers API access to vehicle-state data: diagnostics, fault codes, battery and fuel health, odometer, and maintenance signals. Vehicle owners consent to and control sharing, so builders get data with clear provenance. DIMO adds vehicle-state depth on top of GPS tracking; it doesn't replace it."
}
